WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.819
Turning down a job opportunity?

00:00:01.819 --> 00:00:04.420
Accidentally auditioning for a porno?

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.730
Marrying her ex while she's still with Leonard?

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.680
Believe it or not, these weren't the worst
choices Penny made on "The Big Bang Theory."

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:15.140
Stick around, because we're about to reveal
her most regrettable decision.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:19.730
Kaley Cuoco's Penny goes through quite a lot
during her long run on "The Big Bang Theory."

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:23.810
During the show's tenure, she makes several
major moves to change the direction of her

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:25.269
often chaotic life.

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:29.649
She switches ambitions and goals, manages
to endure the nonstop shifts in her relationship

00:00:29.649 --> 00:00:33.540
with Leonard, gains real friends in the form
of Leonard's friends, and even manages to

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:38.970
make a reliable friend group of her own with
her eventual besties Amy and Bernadette.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.940
All that said, thanks to a tendency to be
impulsive with her decision-making, not all

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:46.390
the choices Penny makes in her life are smart
or good for her.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:47.770
"I get it, I screwed up.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.410
Is this all we're gonna talk about the rest
of the day?"

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:50.440
"Why are you mad at me?

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.829
You're the one that did the stupid thing,
I'm just trying to fix it!"

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:58.260
Before the show begins, she marries her ex-boyfriend
Zack in Las Vegas and never realizes the "joke"

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.175
ceremony was real, forcing her to seek an
annulment from her ex so she can marry Leonard in Season 7.

00:01:04.175 --> 00:01:08.789
After all that, she still agrees to elope
to Las Vegas with Leonard in Season 9 — a

00:01:08.789 --> 00:01:13.079
completely impulsive gesture that cuts their
family and friends out of the equation and

00:01:13.079 --> 00:01:16.990
forces them to orchestrate a bigger private
ceremony later on.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:21.380
Also, incredibly, after insisting she doesn't
want to have kids for the entirety of the

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:26.650
show's run, in Season 12, she ends up pregnant
by Leonard thanks to a birth control mishap.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:31.009
In short, Penny's made a lot of questionable
decisions and has dealt with the fallout,

00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:35.880
but one decision stands above the rest as
arguably the worst one she ever makes on "The

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:36.880
Big Bang Theory."

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.689
Yes, in spite of every other tough choice
in her life, Penny's decision to give up her

00:01:40.689 --> 00:01:45.380
dreams of being a successful actress is still
the hardest one for fans to take.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:49.759
Her life as a working actress is what drives
the character from Season 1 to Season 8.

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:53.689
It's why she moves to California from Nebraska
in the first place and ends up living next

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:55.149
door to Leonard and Sheldon.

00:01:55.149 --> 00:01:59.049
While her acting career definitely has its
ups and downs — including an embarrassing

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:03.249
incident in which she shows up for a cat food
commercial and finds out it's an audition

00:02:03.249 --> 00:02:07.990
for a pornographic film — she seems to weather
these bumps with grace in the hope of making

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:09.720
her dreams come true.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:13.570
For much of the show, this means that she
has to live a few inches above the poverty

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:17.550
line while bartending and waiting tables at
the gang's local Cheesecake Factory.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.451
"Guys, guys, you're never gonna believe this."

00:02:19.451 --> 00:02:20.451
"What happened?"

00:02:20.451 --> 00:02:22.530
"I just got a part on a TV show!"

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.260
But after quitting The Cheesecake Factory
to focus on her acting career in Season 7's

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.910
"The Hesitation Ramification," Penny experiences
extreme embarrassment when her role in an

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:36.110
"NCIS" episode is cut after she tells her
family and friends to tune in and watch her.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:40.450
Her confidence in her acting dreams is shaken,
and though there's hope she might land a role

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:44.920
in the new "Star Wars" film thanks to Leonard's
support, she switches vocations and becomes

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:48.680
a sales representative for Bernadette's pharmaceutical
company in Season 8.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.320
"The Big Bang Theory" generally portrays this
as a positive career move for Penny, who climbs

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:58.195
the corporate ladder and is such a good rep
that she's nearly scooped up by Bernadette's competitor.

00:02:58.195 --> 00:03:02.650
But it's not a job she shows any particular
passion for, even though her apparent natural

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:05.880
skill in the role definitely gives her a confidence
boost.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.400
That said, she ultimately has no real emotional
attachment to the job and nearly leaves it

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.150
when Zack offers her another career opportunity
in Season 10 — which she doesn't take because

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.500
the idea upsets her new husband, Leonard.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:22.010
As tough as her acting career is to maintain,
Penny shows both a passion for acting and

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.210
an aptitude for it throughout "The Big Bang
Theory."

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:28.530
She may make more money in pharmaceuticals,
but there's never a sense of joy and triumph

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:33.130
like the kind she experiences when her performance
in a play draws an emotional response from

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:36.180
her friends in Season 6's "The Monster Isolation."

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:40.150
While Penny seems pretty happy with her life
by the time "The Big Bang Theory" wraps up

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:44.840
its run, fans still consider her career shift
a step backwards for the character.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:48.980
It definitely takes some excitement out of
her storyline, making the career swap the

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:51.340
worst choice she made on the show.

